      "message": "Publisher: keep watching through queued states; post each result comment once\n\nThe Lean-checkpoint watcher (live_publish.watch) failed at 2026-10-20 20:47:59Z\nwith 'Untrusted verification workflow': between the select job and the check\njob, GitHub showed the verify run as queued, and validate_run_identity accepted\nonly in_progress or completed while running. With allow_running it now also\naccepts queued, waiting, pending and requested; a completed-only check is\nunchanged.\n\nThe same toggle sends a second workflow_run in_progress event, so a second\nwatcher sees the same checkpoint (the double checkpoint comments on #16, #18\nand #26). submissions.comment_once posts a result comment only when no bot\ncomment already links the same receipt artifact (bounded to ten pages of\ncomments); the issue checkpoint, the PR result and the final issue comment use\nit. No Actions concurrency group (AGENTS.md: fork YAML can name one).\n\nTests: running states, and one comment per receipt (another receipt or a\nperson's quote does not count; the scan is bounded).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
